KONOHAGAKURE — ABURAME CLAN INSECT-USE POLICY

The Aburame clan hosts colonies of kikaichu (destruction bugs) within their bodies from birth, forming a symbiotic relationship used for tracking, sabotage, and chakra drainage.

Provisions:
- Aburame shinobi feed their colonies chakra; the bond is lifelong and clan-secret.
- Deployment of kikaichu in populated areas requires care to avoid civilian alarm; swarm techniques near non-combatants follow the same restraint as other area techniques.
- The clan maintains breeding records for rare insect strains used in specialized techniques.
- Insect-based reconnaissance data is reported through the normal intelligence chain.

Aburame techniques are clan-restricted knowledge. The quiet, methodical conduct of the clan is a matter of tradition, not aloofness.
Maintained by the Aburame clan head.
